@wip @devflow @concern:rust-style
Feature: Independent spaces reconcile a shared developer discipline
  Developers need reproducible guidance they can use offline; stewards need control over adoption.
  Elohim and Brit encounter each other as independently governed spaces.
  Shared ownership in this exercise confers no cross-space authority.
  A public lesson may travel without exposing private deliberation.
  Local checking, network witnessing and real adoption are separate proofs.

  @act:host
  Scenario: Held discipline remains usable in a standalone offline repository
    Given two isolated spaces hold the same addressed Rust discipline
    And each space explicitly binds that version under its own authority
    When neither the network nor a sibling checkout is reachable
    Then both spaces can materialize and verify their guide
    And each can check its own source against its adopted discipline

  @act:host
  Scenario: Standing changes without rewriting shared meaning
    Given Elohim and Brit refer to the same policy artifact
    When Brit proposes a different local rollout and application scope
    Then the shared artifact address remains unchanged
    And Elohim's effective binding remains unchanged
    And Brit's proposed binding is not effective before its acceptance

  @act:host
  Scenario: Discovering a successor grants neither adoption nor execution
    Given Brit has adopted one verified policy version
    When Brit discovers a successor with a checker it has not admitted
    Then the existing policy continues to govern Brit
    And the successor's executable is not run
    And its proposal and missing admission remain visible

  @act:host
  Scenario: A sole steward delegates two separately grounded repository representatives
    Given one steward authorizes a bounded developer-discipline council
    And each representative starts from its own repository root in a fresh context
    And the steward's imagodei linkage is explicitly unresolved
    When the representatives exchange public positions and evidence
    Then neither receives the other repository's private deliberation
    And two agent seats are not counted as two human stewards or demographic diversity
    And local delegation is not presented as peer-witnessed authority

  @act:host
  Scenario: An exhausted council preserves disagreement
    Given the steward authorized at most two reconciliation rounds
    When the repository representatives remain in disagreement after both rounds
    Then neither representative declares consensus
    And the unresolved positions return to the steward

  @act:host
  Scenario: An encounter helps the receiving space form a workable transition
    Given separate agents represent the two spaces with disclosed fixture context
    And Brit must preserve its inherited Gitoxide compatibility obligations
    When the agents exchange an offer and a counterproposal
    Then the receiving space obtains an evidence-backed bounded trial
    And the trial names its source scope, comparison baseline and rollback conditions
    And the trial preserves upstream-owned source bytes
    And its checks measure inherited debt, refuse a new unexplained suppression and accept an explained exception
    And dissent and local adaptations remain attributable
    And fixture acceptance is not recorded as real steward acceptance

  @act:host
  Scenario: A damaged mandatory dependency cannot silently remove a rule
    Given Brit binds a mandatory addressed policy
    When its held artifact bytes fail address verification
    Then the policy is reported as unverifiable
    And checking cannot report that the governed source passed

  @act:household
  Scenario: A remote peer verifies the receiving space's adoption
    Given two peers represent separately authorized governed spaces
    When Brit adopts an exact offered policy version through its own authority
    Then a receiving peer independently verifies the witnessed adoption
    And the artifact CID and adoption entry and action hashes remain distinct
    And Elohim cannot bind Brit by authoring a declaration of its own

  @act:household
  Scenario: Withdrawal survives reconnect without destroying prior evidence
    Given a receiving peer has witnessed Brit's adoption
    When Brit withdraws that adoption while the receiving peer is disconnected
    And the receiving peer reconnects
    And an unauthorized peer offers a forged lifecycle link
    Then the effective binding reflects the authorized withdrawal
    And prior evidence remains bound to the version and inputs it measured
    And a forged lifecycle link cannot withdraw or reactivate the binding

  @act:host
  Scenario: Brit's committed source must pass its own adopted check
    Given Brit has a committed violation and an uncommitted repair
    And Elohim has a green check over different source inputs
    When Brit requests publication of the committed source
    Then neither the working tree repair nor Elohim's result satisfies Brit's gate
